Derived work
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of utina are derived from bakobo/thesmo (https://github.com/bakobo/thesmo),
Copyright 2026 Bakobo, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

thesmo is a deliberately blind implementation of the Custos specification: its
implementers read the ratified specification and nothing else, so that where two
independent readings disagree, the disagreement is evidence about the document
rather than about the readers. utina is not blind and makes no such claim. Where
utina carries a reading pinned by thesmo, it carries it because that reading is
defensible, not because it was independently derived here.

Specific provenance is recorded per module in the source. As of this writing:

  - The finding codomain, the closed appraisal triple, the transition system and
    the two upward currents derive from thesmo's `m1-alpha` reading of the
    finding-codomain chapter.
  - The byte-canonical encoding derives from thesmo's `m1-beta` reading.
  - The canonical-order log walk derives, as an algorithm rather than as source,
    from thesmo's `m2-gamma` reading of the GEL grammar chapter.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Specifications implemented, not redistributed
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Custos (https://github.com/Nicholas-Keystate/custos) is licensed by its author
under the Community Specification License 1.0. utina implements it. No part of
the specification text is redistributed here; citations in comments and
documentation identify spans by line for the reader's benefit.

The KERI, ACDC and CESR specifications, and the dossier specification
(https://github.com/trustoverip/kswg-dossier-specification), are likewise
implemented or referenced rather than redistributed.
